{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>The butler of the king of Egypt sinned.</b> This one mixed water into wine, and this one mixed ground natron stones into flour. Rashi's explanation: a fly was found in his goblet of lukewarm wine. The scribes' reading is 'פושרין,' for it is written in the Arukh that a cup is called in Greek פוטירי and פיילי. Rather, it is obvious that it is פוטירין, and so it is in Bereishit Rabbah: the chief butler — a fly was found inside his goblet of פוטירין."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {0 "The comment attributes to Rashi the fly-in-goblet explanation; the subsequent discussion concerns the correct reading of the word פושרין vs. פוטירין. I read 'טע׳ סופרים' as an abbreviation for 'טעמא דסופרים' (the reading/reasoning of the scribes) and rendered accordingly."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:05.008807559Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}